# 117 - the stronger form of 116: a skipped right operand cannot fail at all.
# The divide-by-zero (a Value error) and the undefined function (a Name error)
# are both unreachable, so the program runs to completion. Note the precedence
# in the first line: / is rung 6 and == is rung 3, so the rhs is (1 / 0) == 0,
# a Bool-typed expression that would be well typed and still explode.
--- source
print false and 1 / 0 == 0;
print true or nope();
print "survived";
--- expect
false
true
survived
